WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.203
Woo, good shot, Sonta!

00:00:05.203 --> 00:00:05.904
Going down.

00:00:05.904 --> 00:00:08.339
That was distance right there. Thanks.

00:00:08.339 --> 00:00:10.408
Was that your last shot
you hit it on? Second.

00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:11.075
Second, huh?

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:12.710
Yeah. That was out there.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.145
That was a good reach.

00:00:14.145 --> 00:00:16.080
I felt like that was going to happen.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.548
I wasn't quite sure and then.

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:18.316
Oh, yeah.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:20.585
You know, once it starts going down
it's a good feeling.

00:00:20.585 --> 00:00:21.953
That's a good boy.

00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:23.087
Good boy!

00:00:23.087 --> 00:00:25.323
Some dogs, they'll get a couple of goose.

00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:27.625
They might get a little intimidated
because they're so big. Right.

00:00:28.226 --> 00:00:30.061
Doesn't seem to back down from them.

00:00:30.061 --> 00:00:32.096
No he's loving it out here right now.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.564
I just want to make sure

00:00:33.564 --> 00:00:36.501
to capitalize on this time
and get as many birds as we can.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:39.871
Two guns is better than one. Yep.

00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:42.206
Two of us shooting, double our chances.

00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:44.742
I'm done hunting
when our freezers are full,

00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:48.046
so we're going to get it done
and get as many geese as we can.

00:00:54.686 --> 00:00:57.422
It's a hell of a journey today.

00:00:58.356 --> 00:01:01.726
Feels good to reach the goal, you know.

00:01:02.694 --> 00:01:06.197
Yeah cause the river threw
pretty much everything it could at me.

00:01:07.298 --> 00:01:10.435
It's kind of just frozen at this point.

00:01:11.436 --> 00:01:11.970
You know,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.539
you always want things
to just work perfectly,

00:01:15.139 --> 00:01:17.709
and you end up having to go through

00:01:18.209 --> 00:01:21.279
hell and high water, but super grateful.

00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:24.048
Ahh it feels nice.

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:27.552
So at this point,
I got to get this canoe hung

00:01:27.552 --> 00:01:30.221
up, tied up high to one of these trees.

00:01:32.223 --> 00:01:34.792
Come back in early fall,

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:37.895
bring the rifle, bring java

00:01:39.931 --> 00:01:43.868
and we just float down the river.

00:01:53.478 --> 00:01:54.278
I'm frustrated.

00:01:54.278 --> 00:01:56.447
I can't find this buoy.

00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:57.448
Where's that damn thing at?

00:01:57.448 --> 00:02:01.085
It should be like, right in here.

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:03.888
I'm just gonna put a weight on here
in the bottom of it.

00:02:03.955 --> 00:02:05.123
Drag this thing around.

00:02:05.123 --> 00:02:08.760
If I can go crossways to the currant
maybe we can hook on to the line

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.495
if that buoy is like ten feet under.

00:02:21.105 --> 00:02:21.372
The good

00:02:21.372 --> 00:02:24.976
thing about it is the hooks
made out of wood, bone and spruce fruit.

00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:28.413
We harvested the material
to make these hooks from nature.

00:02:28.679 --> 00:02:30.982
They went back to nature.

00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:35.019
Well, lets pull that rope in
and head back.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.588
Alaska's tough.

00:02:37.622 --> 00:02:39.857
Alaska took my halibut hook.

00:02:39.857 --> 00:02:42.393
Alaska's taken some of my friends.

00:02:42.393 --> 00:02:46.297
But Alaska is also given us everything
that we possibly need

00:02:46.798 --> 00:02:50.268
to thrive and survive here.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.070
It's an amazing place,

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.706
but you got to treat it with respect.

00:03:03.748 --> 00:03:05.983
Well, I think it's done, Jeff.

00:03:05.983 --> 00:03:08.086
This is what we live for.

00:03:08.086 --> 00:03:09.420
That's a beauty.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.489
There it is.

00:03:11.889 --> 00:03:12.490
Mmm-hmm.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.358
I'm hearing birds.

00:03:14.358 --> 00:03:17.595
Better make that quick, buddy.

00:03:25.069 --> 00:03:26.104
Look how low.

00:03:29.073 --> 00:03:31.275
We'll grab our goose
and bring it into the blind with us,

00:03:31.275 --> 00:03:34.512
and we can snack on it while we're
hunting. Let's get in there. All right.

00:03:36.214 --> 00:03:37.048
We feel a lot

00:03:37.048 --> 00:03:40.384
more secure when we have birds
heading to the freezer.

00:03:40.918 --> 00:03:43.621
Just a great time to be around a
campfire a little bit,

00:03:43.621 --> 00:03:45.556
do some hunting at the same time.

00:03:45.923 --> 00:03:49.427
We enjoy eating what we're shooting.

